From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shipwright <shipwright@invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report connected hosts and allow taking over the audio route

With Apple's Device ID on both hosts, AirPods stay connected to two
hosts at once and hand audio to the one that asks. Add the multiDevice
capability:

- hosts: the hosts the headphones report as connected (packet 0x2E);
- ownsConnection: whether this host has the audio route (control
  command 0x06);
- {"takeOver": true} asks for the audio route (control command 0x06,
  value 1).

Like the hearing features, it is listed as {"unavailable": "needs Apple
Device ID"} while the host lacks Apple's Device ID.

Protocol reference: LibrePods (https://github.com/librepods-org/librepods),
README "Multi-device Connectivity", docs/control_commands.md,
docs/opcodes.md and the Android AACPManager.kt.

The control command 0x06 (OwnsConnection) and the 0x2E packet parser
(AapConnectedHosts) are added here, with their self-tests in
TestsAapAppleGated.
