+##### Multi-device
+
+Listed for all AirPods and Beats; which models keep two hosts at once is not
+verified. With Apple's Device ID on both hosts, the headphones
+stay connected to two hosts at once, for audio and control, and hand audio to
+the one that asks. `hosts` lists the hosts connected to the headphones, as the
+headphones report them (they send it when it changes); `ownsConnection` says
+whether this host currently has the audio route. Set `takeOver` to `true` to
+ask for the audio route (control command 0x06, "owns connection").
+
+```json
+{
+  "multiDevice": {
+    "readonly": false,
+    "hosts": ["AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF", "11:22:33:44:55:66"],
+    "ownsConnection": false
+  }
+}
+```
+
+```json
+{"method":"SetCapabilities","arguments":{"address":"AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF","capabilities":{"multiDevice":{"takeOver":true}}}}
+```
+
